      "content": "you said \"ethnic homogeneity often aids in national unity and political stability\"—so basically you're saying that because this region is so diverse, it's inherently more prone to the kind of chaos seen in other multi-ethnic developing nations? if we're talking real-world risk, would an investor be right to assume that a diverse demographic like this is a structural disadvantage for staying stable compared to a more uniform population?",
